# Isolated negative control: auditor-stall-watchdog torn-down assertion
#
# Purpose: prove the repaired assertion still detects a worker that is NOT
# cancelled, and that it no longer depends on the child having booted far
# enough to install its own SIGTERM handler.
#
# Disposable copy (/tmp/glla-stall-control, since removed). Two guard removals:
#   1. signalWorkerTree() is never called (no SIGTERM, no SIGKILL escalation)
#   2. removeAuditJobDirectory() is never called (incomplete scratch left behind)
#
# RESULT -- correctly FAILS, for the intended behavioral reason:
#
#   error: timed out waiting for: the detached silent worker was cancelled
#          (handler ran, or the job was reaped)
#   (fail) stall: worker that never emits a first event is failed fast, not
#          left for the wall [22638.19ms]
#    0 pass
#    1 fail
#
# Live source in the repository passes the same test (see final gate logs), and
# the unmodified suite still asserts cancellation -- only the host-dependent
# marker is no longer the sole accepted symptom.
